--- Bonus enemy redesign (Test 38-40) ---
Problems found across the earlier revisions, all reported from actual play:
(1) isBonus exempted the bonus enemy from Enemy.cs's "formation moves its own
members" guard, so it fell through to Enemy.cs's own lane-descent Update()
and visibly traveled straight down instead of side to side; (2) it was
colored gold correctly in code, but still looked red the whole time it was
alive (see the separate color note below); (3) an attempt to keep it
"behind" the row by excluding it from the group's own edge check and
clamping its position meant direction never reversed if it ended up the only
enemy left alive - it got stuck pinned against the boundary; (4) a later
attempt folded it fully into the group's shared direction/edge-check/step-
down cycle, which fixed the stuck bug but introduced a new one - it visibly
paused its sideways motion and dropped straight down every time ANYONE
reached an edge, including itself (far more often than the rest of the group,
since it's the fast one), which read as "stopping" rather than smoothly
sweeping back and forth.

The version below solves "start behind the row" with a short SPAWN DELAY
(not a spatial offset), and then makes the bonus enemy's movement completely
INDEPENDENT of the group once it exists - its own direction, its own edge
bounce, never waiting on or affecting the regular formation's own cycle.
That's what lets it move smoothly and continuously, pass the rest of the row
whenever its speed carries it there, and never get stuck - it never depends
on any other enemy, alive or not, to tell it when to reverse.

