--- Bonus enemy color (reported red instead of gold) ---
This is a SEPARATE bug from the movement one above, also reported from actual
play: the bonus enemy's SpriteRenderer.color was being set to gold correctly
in every pass of this fix, but it still showed up red the whole time it was
alive, only flashing gold for an instant when destroyed. Cause: SpriteRenderer
.color MULTIPLIES a sprite's existing pixel colors - it can't add a channel
that isn't there. If the Enemy prefab's base sprite is baked red (not a plain
white/gray shape), no tint value can ever make it read as gold; a plain white
sprite is required for color tinting to produce an arbitrary color. The hit
flash (Enemy.cs's HandleHit(), see FIRST-PASS below) already swaps to
flashSprite for an instant, which is why THAT moment showed true gold - if
your Enemy prefab's flashSprite field is assigned to a white/uncolored
sprite, that's the same asset the fix above now reuses as the bonus enemy's
permanent base sprite, not just its hit-flash. If flashSprite isn't assigned,
or points to a colored sprite itself, this fix won't produce gold either -
assign it to a genuinely white sprite asset first.

