--- Wave transitions leaving leftover enemies / premature wave end ---
Reported from actual play: destroying the bonus enemy sometimes ended Wave 2
and started Wave 3 while real Wave 2 enemies were still visibly on screen -
which also meant enemiesRemaining could reach 0 (triggering a win) with
enemies still alive. Two compounding causes, both fixed below:

(1) GameManager's wave-advance code (Update(), the nextWaveRequested block)
has never called EnemySpawner.ClearEnemies() before spawning the next wave -
only ResetGame() (restart) did. In NORMAL play this was invisible, because by
the time enemiesRemaining reached 0, every actual enemy really was gone. It
only becomes visible once (2) below can leave an uncounted extra enemy alive.

(2) The bonus enemy's spawn is delayed (SpawnBonusEnemy(), a Coroutine -
see above). If a wave ends, or the player restarts, WHILE that delay is
still counting down, ClearEnemies() only destroyed actual GameObjects - it
never canceled the pending Coroutine. That Coroutine still fired later
regardless, spawning an ORPHANED bonus enemy into whatever wave happened to
be running by then. That enemy was never part of the new wave's own count,
so killing it decremented enemiesRemaining for a wave that never actually
accounted for it - ending that wave one kill early, with real enemies from
it still on screen.

