--- Canvas (Inspector only, no code) - fixes the off-screen HUD ---
Likely cause: the Canvas's Canvas Scaler is set to its Unity default
(Constant Pixel Size), which positions UI elements using raw pixel offsets
from a corner - correct only at the exact resolution it was set up at. Once
Default Screen Width/Height (Player Settings) or the Game view's aspect
changed, those offsets no longer land in the same place, and can push the
HUD partly or fully off-screen.
  1. Select the Canvas GameObject, find its Canvas Scaler component.
  2. Set UI Scale Mode = Scale With Screen Size.
  3. Set Reference Resolution = 1280 x 720 (matches the Build Guide's
     Default Screen Width/Height).
  4. Set Screen Match Mode = Match Width Or Height, slider at 0.5.
  5. Select ScoreText, LivesText, and WaveText one at a time and fix BOTH
     their Anchor AND their Pivot (the X/Y fields right under the Anchor
     Presets icon) - clicking an Anchor Preset alone does NOT move Pivot,
     so if Pivot is still Unity's default (0.5, 0.5, dead center) while
     Anchor is now a corner, Pos X/Y no longer means what it looks like it
     means and the object straddles the edge instead of sitting inside it.
     This IS what was happening: with anchor=top-left, pivot=center (0.5),
     height=95, and Pos Y=-45, the box's top edge sits at -45+47.5=+2.5 -
     just above the screen's top edge. Same story on all three (they all
     shared Y=-45), and LivesText's width/Pos X put its right edge exactly
     ON the screen edge (-120+120=0), leaving no room for its number.
     Fix: in the Anchor Presets picker, hold Shift+Alt while clicking a
     preset - this sets Anchor, Pivot to match, AND position together.
     (Shift alone sets Pivot to match; Alt alone only sets position.) Or
     type Pivot X/Y by hand to match Anchor (0 for left/top, 1 for
     right/bottom, 0.5 for centered). Confirmed working values (Size is
     unchanged from what you already had - not the bug, listed here just
     so every number on these three objects is in one place):
       ScoreText:  anchor top-left    pivot 0/1    size 370x95  Pos X  20  Pos Y -20
       WaveText:   anchor top-center  pivot 0.5/1  size 370x95  Pos X   0  Pos Y -20
       LivesText:  anchor top-right   pivot 1/1    size 240x95  Pos X -20  Pos Y -20
     Once Pivot matches Anchor, dragging or editing Pos X/Y holds at any
     resolution; it's only unreliable to drag-and-fix BEFORE Pivot matches
     Anchor.


